{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>From the Sea of Reeds to the sea of the Philistines.</b> The Sea of Reeds is to the south; the sea of the Philistines is to the west — it is the Great Sea, and it is the boundary of the land of Israel. And so it is written (Joshua 1:4): ״עד הים הגדול מבוא השמש יהיה גבולכם״ — 'unto the Great Sea, the going down of the sun, shall be your border.' And the Great Sea is not the Ocean Sea, for the Ocean Sea surrounds all the inhabited world; and 'from the desert' is to the east; and 'unto the river' is the Euphrates, to the north."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:03:23.928833719Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}